  Scenario: A partial refund updates the order correctly
    Given there is a connect webhook signature for the mock payload "stripe/connect/charges/refund-partial-success.json"
    And there is a POST consumer at "https://api.stripe.com" for "/v1/application_fees/fee_zzzzzzzzzzzzzz/refunds" that will return "stripe/application/refund-partial-fee.json" with status 200
    And there is a GET consumer at "https://api.stripe.com" for "/v1/balance/history/txn_zzzzzzzzzzzzzz" that will return "stripe/connect/balance/refund-partial-transaction.json" with status 200
    And I make a POST request to the API endpoint "/admin/webhooks/connect" as "connect" with the mock "stripe/connect/charges/refund-partial-success.json"
    Then there should be a 200 response from the "connect" request that contains:
      | result    |
      | OBJECT_ID |
    When I am logged in with the "webhooks-connect-refund-one@venzra-test.io" admin account
    And I make a GET request to the API endpoint "/admin/orders/{{ orders[2]._id }}" as "order"
    Then there should be a 200 response from the "order" request that contains:
      | _id       | customer | reference    | items    | shipping                              | destination | billing | payment | history  | status     | created   | updated   |
      | OBJECT_ID | OBJECT   | "2222222222" | ARRAY[1] | { "name": "Example B", "price": 200 } | OBJECT      | OBJECT  | OBJECT  | ARRAY[0] | AUTHORISED | DATE_TIME | DATE_TIME |
    And the response path "payment" from the "order" request contains:
      | reference                 | transaction                  | name        | card   | brand | fee                                                                                                                                      | value | refund |
      | ch_refund_partial_webhook | txn_zzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzz | Example Two | "1234" | Visa  | { "venzra": { "amount": 15, "currency": "gbp", "refund": 4 }, "gateway": { "amount": 27, "currency": "gbp", "refund": 5 }, "total": 33 } | 250   | 175    |

